<Base title="About Jordan’s collection" active="about"><div class="container reading-page"><a class="back-link" href={withBase()}>← Explore the collection</a><h1>My collection.<br /><span class="muted">Community knowledge.</span></h1><div class="prose"><p class="lead">I’m Jordan Davis. This is my personal collection of agent skills, engineering workflows, and developer tools: a single place to explore the components behind better AI-assisted engineering and the ideas I write about.</p><p>The value is in the selection, organization, and practical context—not a claim that I authored everything here. Browse individual skills instead of hunting through entire repositories.</p><h2>Curated across the ecosystem</h2><p>The collection brings together selections from Vercel, ECC, Superpowers, Anthropic, and Supabase, alongside useful tools and a small set of original experimental starters. Each entry explains why it is included, where it came from, and what to consider before using it.</p><h2>Source included or linked upstream</h2><p><strong>Source included</strong> means the selected upstream package is copied without changing its files, with its license and a pinned revision. <strong>Upstream link</strong> means the authoritative package or tool remains with its author. These are different forms of curation, not different ownership claims. <strong>Original starter</strong> identifies new AI-assisted work written for this toolkit.</p><h2>Useful selections, not blanket installation</h2><p>Start with the problem you are solving. Read the instructions and supporting files, check tool permissions, and try a small task in your actual host. Overlapping debugging, planning, and verification workflows are alternatives to compare—not a prescription to activate all of them.</p><h2>Honest evidence</h2><p>The website and snapshot integrity have automated checks. The selected skills have been reviewed as source, not behaviorally evaluated across every agent host. Inclusion does not mean I have used every item in production. Compatibility, performance, and personal-usage claims need their own evidence.</p><h2>Follow the work</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/jdavis-software">My GitHub profile</a> · <a href="https://jdavis-software.github.io/content/">Engineering articles</a> · <a href={withBase('sources/')}>Sources and authors</a></p><h2>Suggest something worth collecting</h2><p>Share the source and the problem it solves in the <a href={`${repository}/issues`}>repository</a>. Read the <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>contribution guide</a> for provenance and evidence requirements. Upstream licenses apply to the copied packages; a license for original repository content remains undecided.</p></div></div></Base>
